   "id": 543767,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "For the following exercise, use Graph <i>A</i> in the given figure. Consider each sequence of vertices. Determine if it is only a walk, both a walk and a path, both a walk and a trail, all three, or none of these.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/04eb7297fb4ca1ee.png\" alt=\"Two graphs are labeled graph A and graph K. Graph A has five vertices: b, c, d, e, and f. Edges connect b c, c f, b d, b e, d e, and e f. Graph K has five vertices: m, n, o, p, and q. Edges connect m n, n o, n q, q o, o p, n p, and m p.\">\n\n<i>d</i> → <i>e</i> → <i>b</i> → <i>c</i> → <i>f</i>",
